<section class="band-raised composability">
  <div class="inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Composability</p>
    <h2>Take what you need. Come back for more whenever.</h2>
    <p>
      Audiorective isn't one big thing you adopt. It's a pile of small,
      independent pieces — take just the clock today, add reactive state when
      you need it, reach for the bindings when a framework shows up. Each
      piece stands on its own, snapping onto a featherweight shared
      <strong>baseplate</strong> only where they need to meet. Even the
      framework bindings are just another brick — your headless engine never
      learns whether React or Vue sits on top. No monolith to swallow, no
      lock-in to regret. Start with one brick. Come back for more whenever you
      fancy.
    </p>
    <div class="lego-mount" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</section>
